Single additive edit; nothing else in the 729-line file changes. Find the exact current tail (lines 728-729):
  "model": "openai/gpt-5.5"
}
Replace with:
  "model": "openai/gpt-5.5",
  "mcp": {
    "basic-memory": {
      "type": "remote",
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:18765/mcp",
      "enabled": true,
      "timeout": 30000
    },
    "agent-mail": {
      "type": "remote",
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:18812/mcp/",
      "enabled": true,
      "timeout": 30000
    }
  }
}
Grounding: opencode's key is 'mcp' (NOT 'mcpServers') per its own $schema (https://opencode.ai/config.json); remote shape is exactly {type:'remote', url, enabled, timeout} with additionalProperties:false — no other fields allowed. URLs copied verbatim from registry SSOT rows (C:/Users/Prekzursil/.agents/agents.json → mcp.servers.agent-mail / .basic-memory), which byte-match the live working .claude.json global mcpServers entries (both servers connected in the current Claude session). Keep agent-mail's trailing slash '/mcp/' exactly as wired — do NOT use the guessed /api/mcp path. No 'headers' needed: registry credentialNames=[] for both (loopback, tokenless). 'timeout': 30000 mirrors registry mcp.policy (startupTimeoutMs/toolTimeoutMs 30000); opencode's default 5000ms is too tight for basic-memory sync search.
